1
00:00:00,697 --> 00:00:01,947
(Sheldon:)Oh no.

2
00:00:02,115 --> 00:00:04,905
- What's the matter?
- I forgot my flash drive.

3
00:00:05,077 --> 00:00:07,207
(Summer:)- So?
- So we have to go back.

4
00:00:07,621 --> 00:00:09,621
Okay, Sheldon, I'm gonna say, "Why?"

5
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:14,040
(Leonard:)And your answer cannot be
"Because I forgot my flash drive."

6
00:00:14,211 --> 00:00:15,291
(Sheldon:)You don't understand.

7
00:00:15,462 --> 00:00:17,922
(Sheldon:)My flash drive has my paper
on astrophysical probes...

8
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:20,220
(Sheldon:)...of M-theory effects
in the early universe...

9
00:00:20,384 --> 00:00:22,974
...I was gonna give to George Smoot
at the conference.

10
00:00:23,136 --> 00:00:25,976
(Leonard:)Why do you have to give your paper
to George Smoot?

11
00:00:26,139 --> 00:00:28,979
(Sheldon:)It's brilliant. He needs to read it.

12
00:00:29,851 --> 00:00:31,981
(Leonard:)So you'll send him an email
when we get back.

13
00:00:32,145 --> 00:00:35,235
(Sheldon:)Then I won't get to see
his face light up as he reads it.

14
00:00:35,399 --> 00:00:38,239
- Right. Of course.
- Oh, this is an unmitigated disaster.

15
00:00:38,402 --> 00:00:41,112
(Leonard:)Well, there's nothing you can do about it,
so relax.

16
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:45,660
(Leonard:)Sit back, enjoy the clickety-clack
of the steel wheels on the polished rails.

17
00:00:50,163 --> 00:00:52,833
[SINGING] You forgot your flash drive
You forgot your flash drive

18
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,500
(Sheldon:)You forgot your flash drive
You forgot your flash drive

19
00:00:55,669 --> 00:00:57,549
(Sheldon:)You forgot your flash drive

20
00:00:57,713 --> 00:01:00,343
Only 10 hours, 55 minutes to go.

